  "facts": [
    "The Nichupté Vehicular Bridge, opened on 2 May 2026, is Mexico's longest bridge, spanning 11.2 km with an 8.8‑km main span over Nichupté Lagoon, cutting travel time from 2 hours 10 minutes to just 10 minutes.",
    "Construction began in August 2022, yet the project doubled its budget from MXN$6.486 billion to MXN$12.021 billion amid technical, environmental, and logistical setbacks before finally opening.",
    "A 103‑meter‑tall metal arch crowns the bridge, making it the second longest water‑crossing bridge in Latin America and a striking landmark visible from the Hotel Zone."
